One word: don't.

Almost all of us that are playing NetHack on an msdos-machine have started
by using this trick. Eventually, we all noticed that this didn't teach us
how to play the game, but actually made our progress slower.

Since there is no real incentive to really try to survive (why bother
being careful if you can just reverse time and try again), you never learn
to play slowly, think about your next move before you make it, etc.

More experienced players, those who manage to do well in the game, almost
all play without ever cheating by using save files. The only way to learn
from your mistakes is when you're actually hurt by making one.

Some newbies, of course, will tell you otherwise, but experience has shown
that those that maintain that save scumming works, also maintain their bad
playing styles, and never make it to ascension.

